olutions","year":1968,"url":"https://www.jstage.jst.go.jp/article/yakushi1947/88/12/88_12_1504/_article","read_scope":"publisher abstract","finding":"Experiments re-examined glucuronic acid/lactone reaction and equilibrium and measured pH and buffer-concentration effects on rate constants.","boundary":"Reaction formula images and numerical rate equations were not evaluated; do not assign plant kinetic constants from this abstract."}],"inference":"This gap warrants an enzyme-independent chemistry review, rather than assuming a missing protein is necessarily required.","next_checks":["Review full experimental conditions and exact D-glucuronic acid/lactone identity","Evaluate rate and equilibrium under relevant plant pH, temperature and compartment conditions","Separate sample-preparation interconversion from endogenous formation","If admitted, create a separate nonenzymatic sensitivity with explicit evidence rather than a characterized-enzyme edge"],"candidate_model_changed":false}},{"source_path":"data/curation/glucuronolactone-fulltext-review.json","source_sha256":"9775582a991064533de0b0db693deac78710e7e9c1494acceafc38c0d69df481","document":{"schema":"cannabis-carbon.reaction-fulltext-review.v1","reaction_id":"balanced-equation:89f51b3b080df52e16249ebab4170dba9bf7f952a9fb8cd79e6633c13ccf9a92","doi":"10.1248/yakushi1947.80.8_1139","source_url":"https://www.jstage.jst.go.jp/article/yakushi1947/80/8/80_8_1139/_pdf","snapshot":"data/raw/glucuronolactone-literature/imai-hirasaka-1960.pdf","snapshot_sha256":"31fc6f9294fcaa3da802dc105a37f8c004f626c1d80da10d7bc7a44ed846f8e0","read_scope":"All four original PDF pages visually inspected; numerical observations below transcribed from Table I on printed page 1141.","observations":[{"starting_material":"lactone","temperature_c":20,"elapsed_value":30,"elapsed_unit":"days","transformed_percent":30,"reported_mean_rate":"1% per day"},{"starting_material":"lactone","temperature_c":50,"elapsed_value":3,"elapsed_unit":"days","transformed_percent":60,"reported_mean_rate":"20% per day"},{"starting_material":"acid","temperature_c":100,"elapsed_value":3.5,"elapsed_unit":"hours","transformed_percent":63,"reported_mean_rate":"18% per hour"}],"kinetic_boundary":"Reported mean transformation rates are not elementary or first-order rate constants. Lactone-starting hydrolysis observations cannot be relabeled as acid-starting lactonization rates. No plant compartment or physiological kinetic parameter is inferred.","additional_findings":[{"location":"printed page 1142, section III","finding":"The authors report that lactone-starting aqueous solutions took nearly ten weeks to reach equilibrium at room temperature; the numerical room temperature is not specified in that passage."},{"location":"printed page 1142, section IV and Table II","finding":"Mineral-acid experiments add an equivalent amount of sulfuric acid and accelerate equilibration. These conditions are not assigned to Cannabis tissue."}],"identity_review":{"location":"printed page 1139, Chart 1","paper_product_depiction":"Cyclic hemiacetal lactone depiction","catalog_product_id":"structure:6cba5bca494bc3beafd63b08de8009a5d1e0f97968aa1fad13668b9ac5914bc4","catalog_product_smiles":"O=C[C@H](O)[C@H]1OC(=O)[C@@H](O)[C@H]1O","catalog_product_depiction":"Open aldehyde side chain attached to the lactone ring","exact_structure_identity_established":false,"required_check":"Resolve cyclic/open-chain and anomeric equilibrium explicitly; do not merge by glucuronolactone name or formula."},"decision":"Retain primary evidence for aqueous nonenzymatic interconversion, but do not promote this exact catalog reaction into the candidate-enzyme baseline. Exact identity bridging and plant-relevant conditions remain unresolved.","candidate_model_changed":false,"proposed_test":"Compare authentic exact-identity standards in enzyme-free and tissue-matrix controls at measured tissue pH and temperature, following time-dependent acid/lactone and cyclic/open-chain species. Inc